  "rationale": "No results yet, so I open the search on the two throughput-friendly families I own. The error constraint (<=2^-10) and the 1 MSPS throughput constraint both push toward moderate data_width and n_iter, while area minimization pulls toward the low end; I bracket data_width 12-16 and n_iter 10-16 to cover the feasible region where accuracy_bits can exceed the 10-bit reference and Fmax can sustain 1 MSPS. I fix rounding to round since it strictly improves accuracy at negligible area cost, and keep angle/frac guards small to hold area down. I split budget 60/40 between pipelined (baseline, best Fmax) and pipelined_m (fewer registers, lower area) to map the area/accuracy trade-off across both."
